{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1165525-canis-minor-faq-pugmire-community-content","id":1165525,"title":"Canis Minor FAQ - Pugmire Community Content!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Partner Worlds","Realms of Pugmire"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-06T00:07:04-08:00","id":1165525,"title":"Canis Minor FAQ - Pugmire Community Content!","content":"Hello, good dogs! As we've talked about on the Kickstarter (and Gen Con, and PAX Unplugged, and Dragonmeet....) we're working on a program to allow people to create and sell Pugmire adventures, along with some other Pugmire-related projects! We're still finishing up the assets, but I wanted to pass along the guidelines and FAQ I wrote. If you have any additional questions or comments, post them here, and I may update the FAQ before it goes live. Thanks!<br /> <br /> <b>\u201cCanis Minor\u201d Program Guidelines</b><br /> <br /> <b>Rules</b><br /> Your work can use any of the game system rules and terms found in the latest edition of Pugmire published by Onyx Path Publishing. You are not allowed to copy large sections of the Pugmire book (over 500 words), aside from material available via the OGL SRD.<br /> <br /> You must include the words &quot;Compatible with Pugmire&quot; or &quot;Requires the use of the Pugmire book&quot; on the cover (front or back), the credits/legal page, and the product description on DriveThruRPG.com.<br /> <br /> <b>Setting</b><br /> You can use any material presented in Pugmire. This includes the names of species, places, locations, masterworks, spells, events, characters, and the like. You can add additional cities and villages within the area referenced in the provided map, but you cannot create new countries, continents, or other locations outside the detailed area.<br /> <br /> At this time, the Monarchies of Mau are not available for use, but will become available when the Monarchies of Mau book is published (at which time this document will be updated).<br /> <br /> <b>Content Restrictions</b><br /> Neither your work nor any advertising, promotions, press releases, or other documents affiliated with the work may contain racist, homophobic, discriminatory, or other repugnant views; objectifying descriptions of people's bodies or cultures; gratuitous depictions or descriptions of violence or gore; rape or other acts of criminal perversion; scenes or material of an explicitly sexual nature; or other harmful or obscene material.<br /> <br /> Neither your work nor any advertising, promotions, press releases, or other documents affiliated with the work may contain any claim that you or the work has been sanctioned or approved by Pugsteady or Onyx Path Publishing, or is affiliated with either company in any way, other than to acknowledge that the work is produced and distributed as part of the \u201cCanis Minor\u201d Community Content program.<br /> <br /> <b>Allowable Media</b><br /> Adventures and limited support products for the Pugmire roleplaying game. You cannot include materials presenting new nations, locations not already detailed, or rules for creating player characters of new species. (Statistics for a non-player character of a previously undocumented species are valid, as long as the entire species is not detailed in the product.)<br /> <br /> Stock art resources for Pugmire adventures and support products, <b>including 3d printer files.</b><br /> <br /> No fiction except short vignettes (750 words or less) in the roleplaying game work. These vignettes must be directly related to the work in question.<br /> <br /> No other media, including but not limited to stand-alone fiction, software, music, and comics, are allowed at this time.<br /> <br /> <b>Art</b><br /> Onyx Path Publishing has made additional stock art and templates available. You can find them here:<br /> <br /> [links to art and templates pending]<br /> <br /> No other art from officially published materials can be used, but you are free to use correctly-licensed stock art or commission your own art for your products (within content restrictions). Photographs are not allowed in any Pugmire product, even if you are licensed to use them.<br /> <br /> The \u201cCanis Minor\u201d logo must appear on the cover of your book at the bottom center or bottom right. It must be discernible and legible at normal full-screen viewing size, but does not need to be the primary logo or title on the cover. You may not use the Pugmire logo, Onyx Path logo, Pugsteady logo, or any other trade dress not released as part of the stock art and templates.<br /> <br /> <b>Legal</b><br /> In addition to the text of the Open Game License, the following text must appear in your product, along with any other legal and copyright information.<br /> <br /> This product was created under license. PUGMIRE and its logo, and CANIS MINOR and its logo, are trademarks of Pugsteady, and used in conjunction with Onyx Path Publishing. All Pugmire setting material, art, and trade dress are the property of Onyx Path Publishing and Pugsteady. <a href=\"http://www.theonyxpath.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.theonyxpath.com</a><br /> <br /> This work contains material that is copyright Onyx Path Publishing and Pugsteady. Such material is used with permission under the Community Content Agreement for \u201cCanis Minor\u201d Community Content. All other original material in this work is copyright [THIS YEAR] by [YOUR LEGAL NAME OR COMPANY NAME] and published under the Community Content Agreement for \u201cCanis Minor\u201d Community Content.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":15,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","user":"eddyfate","date":". 01-04-2018, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","name":"eddyfate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T00:12:28-08:00","id":1165526,"title":"","content":"<b>Frequently Asked Questions</b><br /> <br /> <b>Ownership and License Questions</b><br /> Canis Minor is not an open game license. Beyond what is allowable with the OGL, content creators only have permission to use those unique game systems and background materials explicitly permitted by Canis Minor. Content creators are not allowed to use other material for original content unless they have a license to do so from Pugsteady and Onyx Path Publishing (which requires a separate agreement).<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re still not sure about what you are allowed to publish, check the table below to see if that helps.<br /> <br /> <b>Allowed</b><br /> I want to\u2026<br /> \u2022 design content using the Pugmire rules for Pugmire-related content<br /> \u2022 have my content considered for additional publication by Pugsteady and/or Onyx Path<br /> \u2022 have my content considered for inclusion in digital games<br /> \u2022 have my content considered for inclusion in Pugmire marketing<br /> <br /> <b>Not Allowed</b><br /> I cannot\u2026<br /> \u2022 publish my original IP using non-OGL elements of the Pugmire rules<br /> \u2022 print and sell my Pugmire products on my own<br /> \u2022 publish content for Monarchies of Mau at this time<br /> \u2022 publish crossover games before all the game lines involved are made available<br /> \u2022 publish crossover games with IPs that do not belong to Pugsteady<br /> \u2022 publish my own rules system for games set in the Pugmire world<br /> <br /> <b>Does Pugsteady/Onyx Path own the content that I create in my Canis Minor publications?</b><br /> Yes. Further, content creators are not allowed to create new intellectual property under the Canis Minor program. Rather, every piece of content created uses the Pugsteady/Onyx Path IP. That said, if your work merits incorporation into canon, Pugsteady/Onyx Path will contact you.<br /> <br /> The Canis Minor agreement will grant other Canis Minor authors a license to use your original content at any time from its publication date. <br /> <br /> <b>What do I include in the legal text within my Canis Minor title?</b><br /> We recommend a legal section in this general format:<br /> <br /> This product was created under license. PUGMIRE and its logo, and CANIS MINOR and its logo, are trademarks of Pugsteady, and used in conjunction with Onyx Path Publishing. All Pugmire setting material, art, and trade dress are the property of Onyx Path Publishing and Pugsteady. <a href=\"https://www.theonyxpath.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.theonyxpath.com</a><br /> This work contains material that is copyright Onyx Path Publishing and Pugsteady. Such material is used with permission under the Community Content Agreement for \u201cCanis Minor\u201d Community Content. All other original material in this work is copyright [THIS YEAR] by [YOUR LEGAL NAME OR COMPANY NAME] and published under the Community Content Agreement for \u201cCanis Minor\u201d Community Content.<br /> <br /> <b>If I use content from other Canis Minor authors, do I need to credit them?</b><br /> As more authors contribute to the Canis Minor\u2019s pool of community content, we do not expect to maintain perfect attribution every time some author re-uses elements originally contributed by another author. Such attributions are not strictly required. However, we do think two things would be best practices for all Canis Minor contributors:<br /> <br /> \u2022 When re-using a larger element that you have taken from another Canis Minor author\u2019s work, include a reference to the original work as a link to the DriveThruRPG page within your PDF. For example, if you use a new enemy called the Badger Mystics that you found in another author\u2019s work, you should reference that inside your own work using an internal citation such as &quot;Badger Mystics from Attack of the Badgers by Jane Doe&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u2022 On your title\u2019s credit page, make a list of such references.<br /> <br /> <b>Content and Format Questions</b><br /> <br /> <b>What can I use in my products on the Canis Minor?</b><br /> When you create your own title for the Canis Minor, you get access to a hoard of resources. Your work can use any of the rules published by Pugsteady/Onyx Path. Additionally, Pugsteady/Onyx Path and OneBookShelf will from time to time make additional resources such as stock art, template cover designs, and other such assets available for you to freely use in your Canis Minor titles.<br /> <br /> As others create content for the Canis Minor and expand the world through their titles, you then have access to use that material in turn. All Canis Minor creators contribute to a pool of community content that can be re-used, expanded, and explored by other creators in the Canis Minor community. In short, this is an opportunity to take part in a massive communal design network, one that is officially recognized and sanctioned by Pugsteady/Onyx Path.<br /> <br /> <b>I don\u2019t see anything that would stop me from publishing Monarchies of Mau products on Canis Minor. Can I do that?</b><br /> Not at this time. In the near future, we will announce and update the Content Guidelines as new game settings become available on the Canis Minor. <br /> <br /> <b>Can I create new player character species in my products?</b><br /> No. Pugsteady and Onyx Path reserve the right to product official products featuring new player character species.<br /> <br /> <b>Can I use iconic Pugsteady/Onyx Path characters like Yosha Pug, Pan Dachshund, and Leo Bulldog in my Canis Minor title?</b><br /> Yes. They are good dogs.<br /> <br /> <b>Can I publish comic books, computer games, apps, and so on on Canis Minor?</b><br /> No. For now, we ask that you publish RPG supplements and stock art illustrations only, please. <br /> <br /> <b>Can I sell my Canis Minor title in print as well as PDF?</b><br /> No. At this time, we are not allowing new print files for Community Content programs. If you have questions about this, contact publisher services at <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#38484d5a54514b505d4a4b5d4a4e515b5d4b7857565d5a5757534b505d545e165b5755\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"fd8d889f91948e95988f8e988f8b949e988ebd9293989f9292968e9598919bd39e9290\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a>. <br /> <br /> <b>How do I prepare the PDF of my title for sale?</b><br /> There are many different programs to lay out and prepare your book for digital download. Here are some things to help you make sure your PDF will download properly and look great!<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>[DriveThruRPG tutorial links go here]</i><br /> <b>Fantasy Grounds, Roll20, and Virtual Tabletop Content</b><br /> <br /> <b>Can I publish Fantasy Grounds, Roll20, or other virtual tabletop compatible content through Canis Minor?</b><br /> Yes! As long as your material follows the other posted guidelines, you can produce content for Fantasy Grounds, Roll20, and other virtual tabletop programs.<br /> <br /> <b>What is Fantasy Grounds Content?</b><br /> Fantasy Grounds is a virtual table top (VTT) program published by SmiteWorks that lets you play RPGs virtually with your friends. Now you can do that with Canis Minor content! This lets you play out your favorite community created adventures, monsters, heroes, and other user made enhancements to your game.<br /> <br /> <b>How do I make a Fantasy Grounds file?</b><br /> Most Fantasy Grounds content will be in the form of .mod files created by using the export features from Fantasy Grounds. More information is available in the Fantasy Grounds' Developer Guides: <a href=\"http://www.fantasygrounds.com/wiki/index.php/Developer_Guides\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.fantasygrounds.com/wiki/i...veloper_Guides</a><br /> <br /> <b>How do I upload my Fantasy Grounds compatible content?</b><br /> You upload your content nearly the same way as any other Canis Minor title. On your Account page, click on Enter New Community Created Title, just like you normally would. <br /> When you see the options for &quot;Publish Community Content&quot; or &quot;Publish Fantasy Grounds Content&quot; choose &quot;Publish Fantasy Grounds Content&quot;. This will note your product as Fantasy Grounds compatible, so we can display it in the right places on the marketplace.<br /> <br /> <b>What if I already have a PDF of my title for sale? Can I make a Fantasy Grounds file for it?</b><br /> Yes! But you should then republish the title so that you use the \u201cPublish Fantasy Grounds Content\u201d button per above for the new title listing. Then make private your old listing that was for the PDF-only version using the Edit Title link under My Content on your Account page.<br /> <br /> <b>What logos can I use?</b><br /> The normal artwork rules apply for the thumbnail image/covers.<br /> <br /> For titles with Fantasy Grounds content, you can continue to use the Canis Minor logo, but to make it stand out, you can also use this Fantasy Grounds logo on your cover.<br /> <br /> <b>How do I use these files?</b><br /> For help installing and using files on Fantasy Grounds, take a look at the Fantasy Grounds User Guides here:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.fantasygrounds.com/wiki/index.php/User_Guides\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.fantasygrounds.com/wiki/index.php/User_Guides\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.fantasygrounds.com/wiki/index.php/User_Guides\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.fantasygrounds.com/wiki/index.php/User_Guides </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Can I make a Fantasy Grounds version of another author's Canis Minor release?</b><br /> The artwork, including cartography, that another author includes in their Canis Minor title does not become re-usable by other Canis Minor authors. For this reason, it's likely very challenging to make a Fantasy Grounds compatible version of another author's work without contacting that author and working with them on it as a co-published project. Authors can be contacted by leaving them a message in the Discussion thread of their product.<br /> <br /> <b>Logo and Artwork Questions</b><br /> <b>What kinds of artwork and maps can I use in my Canis Minor products?</b><br /> The artwork (such as illustrations and maps) that you include in your product becomes part of the Canis Minor content that other Canis Minor contributors can then use. Here is general advice for these types of artwork:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Art provided by Pugsteady/Onyx Path. The art you find in the Resources for Canis Minor Creators category is owned by Pugsteady/Onyx Path and can be freely used in your Canis Minor titles. No other artwork from Pugsteady/Onyx Path can be used \u2014 only the art specifically released for Canis Minor Creators.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Public Domain Art. Art that is in the public domain can be used, but it must be listed in the credits.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Stock Art. Usage of stock art depends on the license associated with that stock art. Most of the stock art sold under the Canis Minor Resources category on DriveThruRPG includes a license that would allow it to be used in your Canis Minor titles.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Commissioned Art. You must have all the rights to the art in your project. Commissioned artwork may have not been previously used for any other IP that is not a part of the Canis Minor.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Creative Commons. This depends on the type of Creative Commons license. Some allow commercial use, while others do not.<br /> <br /> <b>What logos are required and allowed on my Canis Minor product?</b><br /> You are required to use the Canis Minor logo on the cover of any product. You may not use the Pugmire logo or any other game line logo as part of your RPG product title.<br /> <br /> <b>Do I have to use the templates provided by Pugsteady/Onyx Path?</b><br /> You are highly recommended to use Pugsteady/Onyx Path templates, but they are not a requirement.<br /> <br /> <b>Payment and Pricing Questions</b><br /> <br /> <b>How should I price my product?</b><br /> When you upload your Canis Minor product, you will enter all the metadata for your product, including setting its price. You have the option to set the price to be free ($0). You can also set the price to be Pay What You Want (PWYW), meaning that each customer can set their own price (from $0 up) to pay for your product. Most products, though, will be priced at a fixed price.<br /> <br /> The ideal fixed price varies with the length of RPG product and its quality of writing, art, and design. Based on historic data from DriveThruRPG sales for PDFs, the most successful price points are $1.00, $2.00, $2.95, $3.95, $4.99, $7.95, $10.00, $14.95, and $19.99.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>How do I get paid?</b><br /> Once you activate your Canis Minor title for public sale, your account will begin to accrue a 50% royalty every time your product sells. You can withdraw your accumulated royalties via PayPal by going to the My Money section of the Account page. Note that the My Money section of your Account page will not display until you have a balance accrued.<br /> <br /> There is a $2 fee to cover the cost of each withdrawal, but you will pay no other fees, either to us or to PayPal, to receive your money.<br /> <br /> To prevent certain types of fraud, we must hold back the amount of royalties you earned in the past 60 days from being eligible for withdrawal. The amount eligible for withdrawal at any time, is your total account earnings balance less the amount earned in the past 60 days. You may use your earnings as site credit to pay for orders on site; this will lower your earnings balance and the amount eligible for withdrawal.<br /> <br /> We pay royalties only via PayPal. Creating a PayPal account is free and easy, and in most countries, you can connect your PayPal account to your bank account and transfer money from PayPal to your bank in a few business days.<br /> <br /> <b>DriveThruRPG Publisher Account Questions</b><br /> <br /> <b>I already have a publisher account at DriveThruRPG. Should I use my normal publisher tools for submitting Canis Minor products?</b><br /> No. Canis Minor products are managed from the My Content section of your Account page on DriveThruRPG.com. Do not use your normal Publisher Hub to set up new Canis Minor products. Royalties for Canis Minor product sales will likewise accrue in your customer account, not in your publisher earnings account <br /> <br /> <b>Can I use my publisher tools on my Canis Minor content?</b><br /> Canis Minor content is associated only with your customer account, not your publisher account. The tools available to you for your Canis Minor content are found on the Account page of Canis Minor. They are a simplified subset of your normal publisher tools.<br /> <br /> <b>Can I release the same products on both Canis Minor and as an independent publisher?</b><br /> Any content created for the Canis Minor, which is completely separate from your other publishing efforts, must remain exclusive to Canis Minor. It cannot be listed anywhere else, and will not be considered part of your publisher account (though it will be part of your \u201cMy Content\u201d on the Canis Minor).<br /> <br /> <b>Other Questions</b><br /> <br /> <b>Can I submit non-English language titles to the Canis Minor program?</b><br /> Please do! You can submit your content in any language.<br /> <br /> <b>Can I submit translated material to the Canis Minor originally published by other creators?</b><br /> Yes, you may translate Canis Minor content with the permission of the original content creator, which will require an agreement between the creator and the translator. This may result in a revenue sharing program as administered by DriveThruRPG.com.<br /> <br /> <b>Can I submit translated material of previously officially published Pugsteady/Onyx Path products?</b><br /> Not at this time. We are in the process of working with professional translation companies.<br /> <br /> <b>Will material be approved by Pugsteady/Onyx Path before it is published on the Canis Minor?</b><br /> There will not be a formal approval process by Pugsteady/Onyx Path or OneBookShelf, per se. However, if you\u2019re found to be breaking our content guidelines, there will be repercussions. For example, your content can be pulled from the site, you might be ejected from Canis Minor as a content creator, and you would receive no payment for copies sold.<br /> <br /> <b>Can anyone rate my Canis Minor content?</b><br /> Only people who purchase your content are allowed to rate and review it. Anyone can join the Discussion on your product page, however.<br /> It is encouraged to keep reviews of other's work positive and helpful, in keeping with the community atmosphere.<br /> <br /> <b>Can I rate my Canis Minor content?</b><br /> No. Self-reviews are not allowed.<br /> <br /> <b>Can I become an administrator for the Canis Minor?</b><br /> At this time, all administration responsibilities are handled by OneBookShelf and Pugsteady/Onyx Path staff.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","name":"eddyfate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T09:42:05-08:00","id":1165599,"title":"","content":"Hi Eddy,<br /> <br /> This sounds awesome. What I'm understanding from this is that Adventure modules are going to be most consistent with the rules and FAQ's above. Also potentially the creation of other artifacts and other items sounds in keeping with these restrictions. <br /> <br /> Can I also clarify that we are allowed to create other towns, cities, or locations within the map provided in the core Pugmire book? For example, I could create a town between Houndton and Pugmire and detail that location?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my products on the ST Vault here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/225678/Dark-New-England-Five-Chronicle-Jumpstarts-Bundle?affiliate_id=235787\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/pro...iate_id=235787</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12515-inclusivegaming","name":"InclusiveGaming","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T01:25:17-08:00","id":1167242,"title":"","content":"Correct! &quot;You can add additional cities and villages within the area referenced in the provided map, but you cannot create new countries, continents, or other locations outside the detailed area.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","name":"eddyfate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T11:07:02-08:00","id":1167712,"title":"","content":"This is awesome Eddy! Thank you! I've got a question about the following two sections:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eddyfate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1165525-canis-minor-faq-pugmire-community-content#post1165525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Allowable Media</b><br /> Adventures and limited support products for the Pugmire roleplaying game. You cannot include materials presenting new nations, locations not already detailed, or rules for creating player characters of new species. (Statistics for a non-player character of a previously undocumented species are valid, as long as the entire species is not detailed in the product.)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eddyfate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1165525-canis-minor-faq-pugmire-community-content?p=1165526#post1165526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Frequently Asked Questions</b><br /> <b>Not Allowed</b><br /> I cannot\u2026<br /> \u2022 publish crossover games with IPs that do not belong to Pugsteady</div> </div> </div> </div>Would either of these be allowable as a non-canon fanworks to our Canis Minor works on this forum or on a personal blog as long as we were not making money off of them?<br /> <br /> <u><b>Example 1 (the more relevant for me)</b></u><br /> For example, I'm a big Planescape fan definitely see Pugmire as one of the many worlds reachable in that campaign. I also run a Tumblr of plot hooks for the setting. If I publish a Canis Minor adventure according to all of the guidelines presented, then on my blog say &quot;here is the very non-canon continuing the adventures way I would tie my work to Planescape. These are some plothooks left unresolved, I'd make these demons server Orcus, and here are the NPCs that may have links to this other world,&quot; would that be kosher from Pugsteady/OPP's point of view?<br /> <br /> <u><b>Example 2 (more idle curiosity) </b></u><br /> Say I were to feature some sentient octopuses in an adventure, not detailed, in accordance with the guidelines. Would I be able to talk about my ideas for the species off of Canis Minor as long as I made it clear they were non-canon and in no way official?<br /> <br /> Thanks again! This is super exciting!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T05:14:32-08:00","id":1169054,"title":"","content":"Example 1: No, because that would be referencing someone else's IP. We only allow people to use the Pugmire setting and their own material.<br /> <br /> Example 2: Yes, that's fine. You can't sell any material on making new species, but if you want to make a Tumblr somewhere detailing your non-canonical notes for playing octopi, feel free!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":15,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","user":"eddyfate","date":".  Edited: Realized my answer to example 1 was slightly misleading, so I edited for clarity. 01-04-2018, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","name":"eddyfate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T21:12:34-08:00","id":1170363,"title":"","content":"One other odd question that I can't see an answer for... what format are allowed? For example, would I be able to publish Pugmire .stl files for 3D printing via Canis Minor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T05:37:18-08:00","id":1172972,"title":"","content":"Hrm, interesting point. Right now, the meta-program (including stuff like DM's Guild and Storyteller's Vault) is really only set up for PDF and Fantasy Grounds files. I will inquire about .stl files, but assume &quot;no&quot; for now. If &quot;yes,&quot; I'll explicitly list that as an option in the final FAQ!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","name":"eddyfate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T08:16:55-08:00","id":1173005,"title":"","content":"Thanks Eddy! That would be really cool if it's a possibility. 3D Printers are on the verge of hitting the mainstream as an affordable utility, so if Canis Minor is compatible with them there is a huge opportunity for trailblazing. I'll be interested to find out. I know DTRPG does host .stl files.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T12:18:27-08:00","id":1173281,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> I looked into it, and it looks like that's something we can offer. So, I've updated my guidelines to allow 3d printer files. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","name":"eddyfate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T02:09:13-08:00","id":1176221,"title":"","content":"A bit disappointing that you're not allowed to make new playable races, because I have some seriously cool ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T06:57:12-08:00","id":1176764,"title":"","content":"So do I! Which is why I'd rather restrict that while I explore official options, at least for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","name":"eddyfate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T10:46:05-08:00","id":1179251,"title":"","content":"This is very exciting, but I'm also really disappointed by our inability to post new playable races or environments. Perhaps you could have a community resource compendium hosted on the same site where you can allow community members to host these things that you don't want to be sold as products in an un-monetizable fashion? That way all these awesome resources could be kept in the same place, but you wouldn't have to deal with two different stat blocks being confusingly sold for a species, or a new location somewhere sold for money that's overwritten with official content.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23762-significantotter","name":"Significantotter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T13:39:26-08:00","id":1179298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Significantotter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1165525-canis-minor-faq-pugmire-community-content?p=1179251#post1179251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is very exciting, but I'm also really disappointed by our inability to post new playable races or environments. Perhaps you could have a community resource compendium hosted on the same site where you can allow community members to host these things that you don't want to be sold as products in an un-monetizable fashion? That way all these awesome resources could be kept in the same place, but you wouldn't have to deal with two different stat blocks being confusingly sold for a species, or a new location somewhere sold for money that's overwritten with official content.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems like something that makes more sense a (hopefully officially permitted) fan project than yet another thing for Eddy to put his effort into setting up. Some kind of fan wiki that collects homebrew from these forums in one place is definitely a good idea, but Eddy has repeatedly made it clear that he has plans for the other races of Pugmire/Mau in the future and I think we need to respect that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11291-tim4488","name":"Tim4488","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T06:15:00-08:00","id":1181108,"title":"","content":"Also, as a note, what's listed here isn't forever. Over time we can (and will) open things up and allow for new ideas. But I need to keep things somewhat constrained to start. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","name":"eddyfate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}